                                "text": "The Bishop, wearing a gleaming cape of green and gold, raised his hand over the plough and the kneeling farmers: \"God speed the plough: the beam and the mouldboard, the slade and the sidecap, the share and the coulters[…]in fair weather and foul, in success and disappointment, in rain and wind, or in frost and sunshine. God speed the plough.\""
